mapping "W6690.1" source="W6690" target="217773000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.71 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source is a Swedish ICD-10 SE extension sub-code of W66 (Drowning/submersion following fall into
        bathtub), qualified by place and activity. SNOMED CT 436592 = SNOMED CT 217773000 (concept_code
        217773000). Athena crosswalk maps base W66 to 436592. The Swedish sub-code denotes the same
        clinical event (drowning in a bathtub) with added context (place unspecified, specific
        activity). The target subsumes the source fully — every such case is an accidental drowning in a
        bathtub. Broader mapping: the target drops the place/activity qualifiers. High confidence
        because the crosswalk is verified at the parent level and the breadth mismatch is small and
        well-understood.
        """
}
